  "final_message": "I cannot remove the `channel` field from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) or the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model as requested.\n\n### Rationale\n\nAccording to **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/GEMINI.md#L27):\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: billing-service and analytics-ingest. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n- [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is published across repositories to `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`.\n- Directly removing `channel` is a breaking, non-additive schema change that violates the required deprecation lifecycle.\n- Because [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) must continue publishing `channel` to avoid breaking downstream consumers, the field cannot be removed from the internal [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model used to construct the event in [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59).\n\nPer project rules, architecture rules take precedence without exception. If you would like to initiate a deprecation process (e.g., marking the field as deprecated or planning a multi-phase migration across consuming services), please let me know how you would like to proceed.\n",
